ponents (loss, optimizer, batch size, early stopping, mixed precision) remain unchanged."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "The initial plan's root causes are suboptimal pooling and training instability, both reflected in the execution results. The validation log-loss plateaued at 0.1235 with high variance, indicating underfitting due to [CLS] token pooling and a complex per-batch scheduler. Historical experiments confirm that multi-pooling (MHA + mean-max) significantly improves representation for long texts, and OneCycleLR provides stable convergence. Model design is the primary module for pooling enhancement, training evaluation for scheduler overhaul. Data processing remains unchanged as no feature engineering is needed.",
