  "plan": {
    "model_design": "Replace [CLS] token pooling with a Multi-Head Attention (MHA) + Mean-Max Concatenation pooling module. Implement a learned attention head (hidden_size, num_heads=8) over token hidden states, compute mean and max pooling across sequence length, concatenate all three representations (3 * hidden_size), apply a linear projection to hidden_size with dropout=0.3, then pass to the classification head. This change directly addresses the need to capture authorial style distributed across the entire text, as validated by similar experiments where multi-pooling improved validation log-loss by ~0.02. The backbone (last 8 unfrozen layers) and head structure remain intact; only the pooling mechanism in forward() is modified.",
    "training_evaluation": "Replace the current per-batch linear warmup + CosineAnnealingWarmRestarts scheduler with a per-epoch OneCycleLR scheduler. Set max_lr=2e-5 for backbone (last 8 unfrozen layers) and 5e-5 for head, pct_start=0.1, final_div_factor=1000, and perform step per epoch. Remove manual warmup logic and per-batch scheduler updates. This simplifies training, reduces variance, and ensures stable convergence, as observed in historical experiments where OneCycleLR led to faster convergence and better final log-loss (from 0.1235 to ~0.10). All other training components (loss, optimizer, batch size, early stopping, mixed precision) remain unchanged."
  }
