ead (intermediate + classifier) with a warmup schedule; Stage 2 unfreezes last 8 layers and continues with OneCycleLR (max_lr=2e-5 for backbone, 5e-5 for head, pct_start=0.1). Replace the current CosineAnnealingWarmRestarts with OneCycleLR to reduce training variance and ensure stable convergence, as observed in successful historical experiments. Also, integrate Focal Loss with adaptive gamma (initial gamma=2.0, increase by 0.5 if val log loss does not improve for 3 epochs, max gamma=4.0) instead of standard CrossEntropyLoss with label smoothing, focusing on hard examples per initial plan.", "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "Replace the current on-the-fly WordNet synonym augmentation with offline pre-computed back-translation augmentation. For each training sentence, generate three augmented versions using Helsinki-NLP OpusMT models (English-to-French, English-to-German, English-to-Spanish to English) with 30% probability. Pre-compute and store augmented texts to avoid memory overhead. This change, informed by historical experiments where synonym augmentation was insufficient and back-translation preserved author style, increases data diversity naturally and addresses the root cause of weak augmentation."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
